    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0456" n="1290" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/594</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Whitehouse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-20T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1149. For Owen [from War
                    Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 73. Legation’s 2760, September 2, 7 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d368-f1"/> The
                    entire number of ships agreed to be chartered to the United States Shipping
                    Board under the terms of the Swedish agreement now having been placed at the
                    disposal of the United States, we have authorized the issuance of bunker
                    licenses for free Swedish vessels in accordance with provision of the Swedish
                    agreement and subject to the rules and regulations of the War Trade Board.
                    Repeat to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
